        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See the family description (<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/64/22\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Basal cell carcinomas</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:38:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124469,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are usually pink papules and plaques that are frequently ulcerated and may have a scar-like presentation. They are most frequent on the head and neck. On dermoscopy they are typified by thin serpentine vessels. Biopsy should include deep reticular dermis for most accurate diagnosis {16681663}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:38:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
